  "question": {
    "text": "The value of the integral $I=\\int_0^1 x(1-x)^n d x$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{n+1}+\\frac{1}{n+2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{n+1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{n+2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{n+1}-\\frac{1}{n+2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\int_0^1 x(1-x)^n d x$\n$-I=\\int_0^1-x(1-x)^n d x=\\int_0^1(1-x-1)(1-x)^n d x$\n$=\\int_0^1(1-x)^{n+1} d x-\\int_0^1(1-x)^n d x$\n$=\\left[\\frac{(1-x)^{n+2}}{-(n+2)}\\right]_0^1-\\left[\\frac{(1-x)^{n+1}}{-(n+1)}\\right]_0^1=\\frac{1}{n+2}-\\frac{1}{n+1}$\n$I=\\frac{1}{n+1}-\\frac{1}{n+2}$"
  }
}